<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marwan II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 750</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marwan II was the last Umayyad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a>, reigning from 744 until his death in 750. He came to power during civil wars and spent his reign fighting internal revolts. He was defeated by the Abbasid revolutionaries at the Battle of the Zab in 750 and killed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> in the east.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marwan-ii.jpg" alt="Marwan II" width="320" height="153" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 8-th century mint masters · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dirham_of_Marwan_II_ibn_Muhammad,_AH_127-132.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
